          %h2#models_in_modal_logics Models in Modal Logics
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semantics"} semantics
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logics"} modal logics
            based on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+frames"} Kripke frames
            (“geometric” in contrast to
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+models+for+modal+logics"} algebraic models for modal logics
            %strong Kripke semantics
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Kripke59"}> Kripke (1959)
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#Kripke63"} (1963)
          %p
            In the following we say
            %em frame
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+frame"} Kripke frame
          %h3#models_in_monomodal_logics Models in Monomodal Logics
          %p Again we look at the basic model language.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %em model
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_\omega(1)
              is a pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔉
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M} = (\mathfrak{F},V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔉
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+%28modal+logic%29"} frame
              (for
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_\omega(1)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo :
                      %mi Prop
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V: Prop \to \mathcal{P}(W)
              = succeed "," do
                %em valuation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              a subset of the set,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %h3#gloss Gloss
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Informally we think of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(p)
                as the set of ‘worlds’ in our model where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is true.
            %li
              %p
                The binary relation of the frame allows for the modelling of the truth of a modal proposition,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⋄
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Diamond \phi
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo □
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box \phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                at related worlds.
          %h2#satisfaction Satisfaction
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              is a state in a model
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M} = (W,R,V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              being satisfied in the model at state
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Prop
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in Prop
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models p
                  if and only if
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi w
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in V(p)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mo ⊥
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \bot
                  never;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \neg \phi
                  if and only if it is not true that
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \phi
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \phi \vee \psi
                  if and only if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models\phi
                  or
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ψ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models\psi
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mo ⋄
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \Diamond \phi
                  if and only if, for some
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in W
                  such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                          %mi w
                          %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R w v
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo ,
                          %mi v
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},v \models \phi
          %h3#notes Notes
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                The terminology used in talking about ‘satisfaction’ tends to interpret
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},v \models \phi
                as saying the formula
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is
                %strong true
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M}
                at state
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo ,
                      %mi w
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mo □
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \square \phi
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall v\in W
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R w n
                implies
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi v
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},v \models  \phi
            %li
              %p
                We say a set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                of formulae is true at state
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in W
                of a model
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \Sigma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                are satisfied as
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            %li
              %p
                It is convenient to extend the valuation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                to arbitrary formulae by setting
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(\phi) := \{w \mid \mathfrak{M},w \models \phi\}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo ⊧
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},v \models  (\phi\to \psi)
                and
                %em modus ponens
                holds, (i.e. we have a logic as such in which we are working, then
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(\phi)\subseteq V(\psi)
          %h3#what_is_a_valuation What is a valuation?
          %p In the definition of a Kripke model the valuation is all important. It is what puts meaning onto the frame. It is very useful to push this idea around through a couple of adjunctions and reinterpretations. The process is fairly intuitive, but it pays to do things reasonably formally:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Note that the power set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(W)
                can also be written as
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                        %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}^W
                the set of functions from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
                for the ‘set’ of classical
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mo →
                        %mo ⊤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\bot \to \top\}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi true
                        %mo ,
                        %mi false
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{true,false\}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
                or … . We wrote ‘set’ in inverted commas for several reasons:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    Firstly an important role here is played by the multiple structures that
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
                    has. It is a
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
                    structure; it is the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
                    in the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                    of sets, and so on. In fact it is the source of most of the logic semantic structure within this context. Its structure induces similar structures on the powerset,
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒫
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(W)
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizing+object"} ambimorphic objects
                    in the entry on the
                    = succeed ".)" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chu+construction"} Chu construction
                %li
                  %p
                    Next note that although we said ‘set’ we could do a lot of this in other settings. For instance we could work within a more general topos with an object of possible worlds and an object of propositions. We would need the extra
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
                    structure on what would there probably be written as
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
                %li
                  %p
                    Finally we could categorify things. For the moment we will leave this aside, but note the discussion at
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            %li
              %p
                For convenience we will write
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Prop
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prop
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo :
                        %mi P
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                          %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V: P\to \mathbf{2}^W
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} currying
                this corresponds to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo :
                        %mi P
                        %mo ×
                        %mi W
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V: P\times W\to \mathbf{2}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo ×
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\times W
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,w)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in V(p)
                so interprets as the set of pairs in which the proposition
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is ‘true’ in world
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            %li
              %p
                We could re
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/currying"} curry
                after transposing
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                to correspond to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo :
                        %mi W
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{V}: W \to \mathcal{P}(P)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde{V}(w)
                is the set of propositions true about the world
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            %li
              %p
                Another useful direction is to see this as giving a binary
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chu+construction"} Chu space
          %h2#models_in_multimodal_logics Models in Multimodal Logics
          %p
            Again we look at the basic model language this time with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            unary modal operators.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em model
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℒ
                      %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_\omega(n)
              is a pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔉
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M} = (\mathfrak{F},V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔉
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{F}
              is a frame (for
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℒ
                        %mi ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L}_\omega(n)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo :
                      %mi Prop
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V: Prop \to \mathcal{P}(W)
              = succeed "," do
                %em valuation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              a subset of the set,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %h2#satisfaction_in_the_multimodal_case Satisfaction in the multimodal case
          %p
            This is virtually the same as in the monomodal case, except for the last case which involves the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            modal operators. (We give it in full repeating the earlier cases for convenience.)
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              is a state in a model
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔐
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M} = (W,R,V)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              being satisfied in the model at state
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Prop
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in Prop
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models p
                  if and only if
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi w
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in V(p)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mo ⊥
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \bot
                  never;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mo ¬
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \neg \phi
                  if and only if it is not true that
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \phi
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \phi \vee \psi
                  if and only if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models\phi
                  or
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ψ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models\psi
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi …
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = 1, \ldots, n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔐
                        %mo ,
                        %mi w
                        %mo ⊧
                        %msub
                          %mo ⋄
                          %mi i
                        %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},w \models \Diamond_i \phi
                  if and only if, for some
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in W
                  such that
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi R
                            %mi i
                          %mi w
                          %mi v
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i w v
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔐
                          %mo ,
                          %mi v
                          %mo ⊧
                          %mi ϕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{M},v \models \phi
          %p
            Satisfaction on a class of models is related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/validity"} validity
            of modal formulae. In this way a class of frames can determine a logic and then the logic determines a class of frames. The axiomatisation of that class/logic is then an interesting challenge.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+frame"}> Kripke frame
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+semantics"} Kripke semantics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+model+for+modal+logic"} algebraic model for modal logic
          %h2#references References
          %p The concept originates with:
          %ul
            %li#Kripke59
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+A.+Kripke"}> Saul A. Kripke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Completeness Theorem in Modal Logic
                %strong 24
                1 (1959) 1-14 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2964568"}> doi:10.2307/2964568
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2964568"} jstor:2964568
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.filosoficas.unam.mx/~morado/Cursos/17Modal/Kripke1959.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Kripke63
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+A.+Kripke"}> Saul A. Kripke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantical Analysis of Modal Logic I. Normal Modal Propositional Calculi
                %strong 9
                5-6 (1963) 67-96 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1002/malq.19630090502"}> doi:10.1002/malq.19630090502
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+A.+Kripke"}> Saul A. Kripke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantical Considerations on Modal Logic
                %strong 16
                (1963) 83-94 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://saulkripkecenter.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Semantical-Considerations-on-Modal-Logic-PUBLIC.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Kripke65
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saul+A.+Kripke"}> Saul A. Kripke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Semantical Analysis of Modal Logic II. Non-Normal Modal Propositional Calculi
                %em The Theory of Models
                (Proceedings of the 1963 International Symposium at Berkeley) Studies in Logic and the Foundations of Mathematics (1965) 206-220 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-7204-2233-7.50026-5"}> doi:10.1016/B978-0-7204-2233-7.50026-5
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#BlackburnDeRijkeVenema01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Patrick+Blackburn"}> Patrick Blackburn
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maarten+de+Rijke"} Maarten de Rijke
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yde+Venema"} Yde Venema
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modal Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 53
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781107050884"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781107050884
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valentin+Goranko"}> Valentin Goranko
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Otto"} Martin Otto
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Model Theory of Modal Logic
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Handbook of Modal Logic
                %strong 3
                (2007) 249-329 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www2.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~otto/papers/mlhb.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://cgi.csc.liv.ac.uk/~frank/MLHandbook/"} book webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/studies-in-logic-and-practical-reasoning/vol/3/suppl/C"} publisher page
          %p
            Generalization beyond
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kripke+frames"} Kripke frames
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dov+Samet"}> Dov Samet
              , §6 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em S5 knowledge without partitions
              %strong 172
              (2010) 145–155 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11229-009-9469-0"}> doi:10.1007/s11229-009-9469-0
              \&amp;rbrack;
